CORE
main.sh

^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[assertion\.1\] file main.sh line 3 assertion "\$\{\?\}" -eq 0: SUCCESS$
^\[assertion\.2\] file main.sh line 5 assertion reached = maybe: FAILURE$
^\[assertion\.3\] file main.sh line 7 assertion "\$\{1\}" != run: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
exec without a command applies redirections to the shell (dash exits if
one fails); exec with a command replaces the shell, so the script does
not continue.
